## summary
  first block after the freeze: frozen 0.838
  worst block (weeks 45-48 after): frozen 0.548, majority-class 0.544, retrained 0.693, persistence 0.865
  blocks with frozen < 0.75: 12 of 20 (weeks 5-8 … 49-52 after)
  retrained beats frozen in 12 of 20 blocks; frozen beats retrained in 7
  persistence range 0.816–0.905 (beats frozen in 19 of 20 blocks)
  KS on frozen scores: first block 0.142, max 0.809, last block 0.325
  Pearson r(KS_score, frozen accuracy) over 20 blocks = -0.853 (p = 1.7e-06)

## robustness: the same protocol with all seven columns (Victoria included)
  all-seven model: Victoria columns reset to their training fill moves its score by up to 0.48 -> it DID learn from the one day of Victoria data in its training year
  all-seven frozen accuracy by block: 0.831 0.632 0.698 0.671 0.666 0.711 0.666 0.624 0.624 0.653 0.608 0.550 0.612 0.833 0.759 0.804 0.804 0.835 0.845 0.795
  all-seven: first 0.831, worst 0.550, r(KS_score, acc) = -0.846, retrained wins 12 of 20
